.TH QDP 1 "2026 April 02" "Qore 2.3" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qdp \- command-line interface for Qore data providers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdp
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIprovider\fP
[\fIcommand\fP]
[\fIargs\fP]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqdp\fR is an interactive command-line tool for querying and managing data
providers.
It supports databases, REST APIs, services, and other data sources through
Qore's DataProvider framework with DPQL (Data Provider Query Language).
.PP
Data providers can be specified as connection names, factory references with
options, or application actions.
Child providers can be navigated with \fB/\fP-separated paths.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Format and Output"
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-json
Use JSON for input and output.
.TP
.BR \-Y ", " \-\-yaml
Use YAML for input and output.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable color output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (repeatable).
.SS "Search and Query"
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-dpql
Use DPQL search expressions.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-expressions
Use legacy search expressions.
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-dpql\-help
Show DPQL syntax help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit =\fIN\fP
Limit the number of results returned.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-offset =\fIN\fP
Skip the first \fIN\fP results.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bulk
Use the bulk API for operations.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-timeout =\fIseconds\fP
Set the operation timeout.
.SS "Execution"
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview changes without executing them.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mapper =\fIspec\fP
Field mapper (inline hash or file path).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-options =\fIspec\fP
Data provider options.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subtype =\fItype\fP
Provider subtype.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host =\fIhostname\fP
Hostname for webhook listeners.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module =\fImodule\fP
Load an additional module (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-servers
Enable background servers.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-show\-required
Show only required fields in output.
.SS "Information"
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-list\-connections
List all known connections.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-list\-factories
List all known data provider factories.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-list\-types
List all known types.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-list\-apps
List all known applications.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-create\-index
Create provider indices.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-pipeline\-help
Show pipeline syntax help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH COMMANDS
Common commands include:
\fBlist\fP, \fBinfo\fP, \fBsearch\fP, \fBcreate\fP, \fBupdate\fP,
\fBdelete\fP, \fBupsert\fP, \fBdorequest\fP, \fBlisten\fP,
\fBinteractive\fP, \fBpipeline\fP, and many more.
.PP
Run \fBqdp\fP without arguments or with \fB\-h\fP for the complete command list.
.SH PROVIDER FORMATS
.TP
.I connection
A named connection from the connection provider.
.TP
.IR factory { options }
A data provider factory with inline options.
.TP
.BI @ app / action
An application action.
.TP
.IB provider / child /...
Navigate a provider hierarchy with path separators.
.SH EXAMPLES
List records from a database table:
.RS
.B qdp mydb/mytable list
.RE
.PP
Search with DPQL:
.RS
.B qdp \-q mydb/mytable search 'name = "foo"'
.RE
.PP
List available connections:
.RS
.B qdp \-c
.RE
